   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Ashok,<div><br></div><div>Unfortunately, <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361100538000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28S-584oIgkSAsp_OOIFpb\">shinyapps.io</a> does not support running scheduled jobs. Applications will automatically wake up when they are accessed, and go to sleep when they are no longer being used. However you may be interested in the <a href=\"https://shiny.rstudio.com/reference/shiny/latest/reactiveTimer.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://shiny.rstudio.com/reference/shiny/latest/reactiveTimer.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361100538000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2AEpYGDaoM7j4VsjANWJRz\">reactiveTimer</a> function inside of shiny.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>-Andy</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
